{
  "requirement": "`languages::PlainText` implements `OutlineLang` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider`. Its default value is\ncheaply cloneable and claims no extensions. The filename-based constructors\nselect it when no supplied language claims the extension, including filenames\nwithout an extension, under {cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.defaults`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The structural obligations of `requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.language` are all met. I did not assess runtime behavior.\n\n- **`OutlineLang` implementation:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/languages/mod.rs` invokes `language!(PlainText, super::plain::PROFILE, \"plain-text-structural-v1\")` (the marked `macro@e44d6e074366` node). The `macro[language]` expansion implements `OutlineLang` for `PlainText`, giving it `name`, `extensions`, `outline`, `fingerprint_scheme` and `search_structure`. This matches the signatures in `requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider`. Its `name` and `extensions` come from the plain-text profile.\n- **Default value:** the macro declares `pub struct PlainText;` with `#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]`. That gives a `Default` value, and `Clone` and `Copy` on a unit struct make it cheaply cloneable.\n- **No claimed extensions:** `PlainText::extensions()` returns `$profile.extensions`. In `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/plain.rs#static[PROFILE]` that is `extensions: &[]`.\n- **Fallback selection:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/contents.rs#impl[OutlineContent]/fn[from_source]` looks the filename up in `languages::registry().for_path`. If no provider claims it, it calls `Self::from_source_with(&languages::PlainText, ...)`. `from_path` and `from_id` go through `from_source`. `profile_for_path` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/profile.rs` also falls back to `plain::PROFILE`. The registry lists only the eight claimed-extension languages, and plain text is not one of them, so a filename with no extension, or an unclaimed one, falls through to `PlainText`. The refining `requirements.sdk.outlines.defaults` is assessed on its own text and is cited here only for context.\n\nTests exist in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs`, for example `bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline`, which asserts the name and empty extensions. They carry `{test}` references to `requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.PlainText`. I found no structural gaps, and there are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments.",
  "references": "d364693a64f673cea5b31c5d57cc4436a3d085824fd398288e275ce0c804733a",
